# Universal DSPy generation vocabulary.
#
# This graph defines law only. It intentionally contains no dspy:Signature,
# dspy:InputField, dspy:OutputField, dspy:Module, dspy:MCPServerConnection,
# dspy:ServerArg, or dspy:Optimizer individuals, so composing this schema pack
# cannot inject any signature, module, or optimizer into a consumer's generated
# src/dspy_program.py / src/dspy_optimize.py. A consumer project supplies its
# own individuals against this vocabulary in its own .ttl.
#
# Covers five of dspy.ai's own tutorials verbatim (fetched/verified 2026-08-10, cross-checked
# against the real installed dspy 3.1.3 source tree, not just docs prose):
#   - Predict/ChainOfThought signatures+modules (general DSPy modeling)
#   - MCP tool use: https://dspy.ai/tutorials/mcp/
#   - GEPA reflective prompt optimization: https://dspy.ai/tutorials/gepa_ai_program/,
#     https://dspy.ai/api/optimizers/GEPA/overview/
#   - RL/GRPO optimization: https://dspy.ai/tutorials/rl_ai_program/,
#     https://dspy.ai/tutorials/rl_papillon/
#   - GEPA worked examples: https://dspy.ai/tutorials/gepa_facilitysupportanalyzer/ (Literal /
#     List[Literal] enum-typed output fields, multiple sibling ChainOfThought modules),
#     https://dspy.ai/tutorials/gepa_trusted_monitor/ (int output field with ge/le bounds)
#
# 2026-08-10: composition/retrieval/KNN/Parallel/Ensemble/KNNFewShot support added. The
# retrieve-then-reason (RAG) pattern, the multi-hop query-gen/retrieve/accumulate/answer-gen
# loop, and dspy.KNN/dspy.Parallel/dspy.Ensemble/dspy.KNNFewShot construction were each
# actually built and executed against the real installed dspy 3.1.3 this session (not assumed
# from docs) -- see dspy:PipelineStep, dspy:ArgBinding, the "MultiHop" dspy:kind, and the
# "Ensemble/KNNFewShot Optimizer properties" section below for what's admitted from each.

@prefix dspy:    <http://seanchatmangpt.github.io/packs/dspy#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix prov:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdf:     <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

# ── Core model ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

dspy:Signature a rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Signature" ;
    rdfs:comment "A dspy.Signature subclass: a typed input/output contract with a docstring, rendered as one class in src/dspy_program.py." .

dspy:InputField a rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Input field" ;
    rdfs:comment "One dspy.InputField on a Signature." .

dspy:OutputField a rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Output field" ;
    rdfs:comment "One dspy.OutputField on a Signature." .

dspy:Module a rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Module" ;
    rdfs:comment """A dspy program instance, one of: bound to one Signature
(Predict/ChainOfThought/ReAct/ProgramOfThought/MultiChainComparison/RLM/CodeAct); wrapping
another Module (BestOfN/Refine, via dspy:wrapsModule); an ordered linear composition of steps
(Pipeline, via dspy:hasStep) or the fixed retrieve-then-reason recipe (MultiHop); or a
retrieval/parallel-execution utility (KNN, Parallel). The generated module constructs but does
not configure or invoke an LM.

RESOLVED 2026-08-10 (previously excluded, see git history): dspy.KNN and dspy.Parallel were
previously excluded here because neither takes a Signature at construction. Both were
actually constructed and run against the real installed dspy 3.1.3 this session with no bugs
found, and are now admitted via dedicated properties (dspy:trainsetName/dspy:usesEmbedder/
dspy:kValue for KNN; dspy:hasParallelStep plus the real execution-tuning kwargs for
Parallel) rather than forcing them into the Signature-bound shape.""" .

dspy:LocalTool a rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Local tool" ;
    rdfs:comment "One plain Python callable passed in a CodeAct module's tools=[...] list. Unlike dspy:MCPServerConnection's dynamically-discovered tools, CodeAct's tools are ordinary local functions -- ggen scaffolds each as a NotImplementedError stub the consumer completes, the same 'construct but do not implement arbitrary logic' boundary as dspy:metricFunction." .

dspy:MCPServerConnection a rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:label "MCP server connection" ;
    rdfs:comment "A stdio-launched MCP server a ReAct Module discovers tools from at call time, per dspy.ai's DSPy + MCP tutorial. Only the launch command/args are admitted; the server's own tool list is genuinely dynamic and is never enumerated as a fixed fact." .

dspy:ServerArg a rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Server launch argument" ;
    rdfs:comment "One ordered positional argument passed to an MCPServerConnection's launch command." .

dspy:Optimizer a rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Optimizer" ;
    rdfs:comment """A dspy optimizer (one of the 16 admitted kinds -- see dspy:kind) that
compiles one target Module via dspy:optimizes, OR (Ensemble only) combines multiple existing
Modules via dspy:hasEnsembleMember with no metric/target-Module concept at all -- Ensemble's
real compile(programs) takes a list, not a single student. The metric/reward function BODY and
trainset/valset/devset are deliberately out of scope -- arbitrary, consumer-owned inputs; ggen
scaffolds a NotImplementedError metric stub and named placeholder datasets in
src/dspy_optimize.py.

RESOLVED 2026-08-10 (previously excluded, see git history and the round-5 comment below):
dspy.Ensemble and dspy.KNNFewShot were previously excluded here. Both were actually
constructed and run against the real installed dspy 3.1.3 this session with no bugs found.
KNNFewShot fits the normal dspy:optimizes shape (its real compile(student, teacher=None) takes
one target Module) and is admitted via dspy:kValue/dspy:trainsetName/dspy:usesEmbedder.
Ensemble does not fit dspy:optimizes at all and is admitted via a dedicated
dspy:hasEnsembleMember property instead -- see the round-5 comment.""" .

dspy:LiteralOption a rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Literal option" ;
    rdfs:comment "One ordered value of a Literal[...] (or List[Literal[...]]) typed field, per the gepa_facilitysupportanalyzer tutorial's Literal['low','medium','high']-style output fields." .

dspy:PydanticModel a rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Pydantic model" ;
    rdfs:comment "A pydantic.BaseModel subclass ggen generates, usable as a Signature field's type (confirmed real and working: dspy.Signature accepts a pydantic.BaseModel-typed field, e.g. `address: Address = dspy.OutputField()`, dspy 3.1.3). A third, mutually-exclusive alternative to dspy:pythonType/dspy:hasLiteralOption on InputField/OutputField." .

dspy:PydanticModelField a rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Pydantic model field" ;
    rdfs:comment "One field of a dspy:PydanticModel, typed with a primitive dspy:pythonType (nested PydanticModel-in-PydanticModel fields are out of scope for this round)." .

dspy:LMConfig a rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:label "LM configuration" ;
    rdfs:comment """A real dspy.LM(...) construction: a model string plus the optimizer-relevant
subset of its real constructor kwargs (verified via inspect.signature(dspy.LM.__init__), dspy
3.1.3: model, model_type, temperature, max_tokens, cache, num_retries, use_developer_role --
train_kwargs/launch_kwargs/callbacks/provider/finetuning_model are out of scope, the same
'arbitrary/non-representable collaborator' boundary as dspy:metricFunction). Referenced by
dspy:reflectionModel/dspy:promptModel/dspy:taskModel instead of a bare model-id string, so real
per-call-site LM tuning (e.g. a cheap classification call using max_tokens=500 vs. an agentic
call using max_tokens=16000 -- a real, load-bearing pattern, not hypothetical) is admittable,
not just the model name. dspy.Module-level LM binding remains deliberately out of scope --
dspy-pack's Modules construct but do not configure or invoke an LM; LMConfig only ever backs an
Optimizer's own real LM-taking parameters.""" .

dspy:PipelineStep a rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Pipeline step" ;
    rdfs:comment "One ordered step of a Module of dspy:kind \"Pipeline\". Either a leaf dspy.Retrieve call (dspy:stepKind \"Retrieve\", no dspy:stepSignature -- verified real shape: dspy.Retrieve(k=3), takes no Signature) or a Signature-bound leaf module (any other admitted leaf dspy:kind, requires dspy:stepSignature) -- both real, running patterns confirmed this session (dspy 3.1.3) via an actually-executed RAG module (self.retrieve(...).passages -> self.generate_answer(context=..., question=...))." .

dspy:ArgBinding a rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Pipeline step argument binding" ;
    rdfs:comment "One kwarg passed to a dspy:PipelineStep's call inside the generated forward(). Its value comes from either the Pipeline Module's own external input (dspy:argSourceKind \"PipelineInput\") or a prior step's output field (dspy:argSourceKind \"StepOutput\", via dspy:argSourceStep) -- this is the real data-flow wiring that makes a linear multi-step dspy program (e.g. the verified RAG pattern's context = retrieve(question).passages -> generate_answer(context=context, question=question)) representable declaratively." .

dspy:ParallelStep a rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Parallel step" ;
    rdfs:comment "One ordered member of a Module of dspy:kind \"Parallel\"'s exec_pairs scaffold -- a reference to an existing dspy:Module. dspy.Parallel's real forward() takes a list[tuple[module, Example]]; the Example half is consumer-owned runtime data (out of ontology scope, the same boundary as dspy:metricFunction), so ggen scaffolds the module list and a placeholder pairs list the consumer fills in." .

dspy:EnsembleMember a rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Ensemble member" ;
    rdfs:comment "One ordered member of an Optimizer of dspy:kind \"Ensemble\"'s real compile(programs) list -- a reference to an existing dspy:Module. Confirmed via real execution (dspy 3.1.3): dspy.Ensemble(reduce_fn=...).compile([m1, m2, m3])() correctly reduces the members' outputs." .

dspy:EmbedderConfig a rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Embedder configuration" ;
    rdfs:comment "A real dspy.Embedder(model, batch_size=200, caching=True) construction, verified via inspect.signature(dspy.Embedder.__init__) against dspy 3.1.3. Referenced by dspy:usesEmbedder (KNN Module / KNNFewShot Optimizer) as the real 'vectorizer' constructor argument both classes require -- the same LMConfig-style 'real collaborator construction, not a bare value' pattern, since a plain string can't represent dspy.Embedder's real shape." .

# ── Signature / field properties ──────────────────────────────────────────────

dspy:className a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Signature ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "Python class name for the generated dspy.Signature subclass. Must be a valid Python identifier." .

dspy:hasInput a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Signature ; rdfs:range dspy:InputField .
dspy:hasOutput a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Signature ; rdfs:range dspy:OutputField .

dspy:name a rdf:Property ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "Python identifier: a field name, a Module's variable name, an MCPServerConnection's variable name, or an Optimizer's variable name, depending on domain." .

dspy:pythonType a rdf:Property ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "One of the admitted primitive types: str, int, float, bool. A field (Signature InputField/OutputField, or PydanticModelField) carries exactly one of dspy:pythonType, dspy:hasLiteralOption, or dspy:hasPydanticModelType." .

dspy:hasLiteralOption a rdf:Property ; rdfs:range dspy:LiteralOption ;
    rdfs:comment "Renders the field as Literal[...] (or, with dspy:isListType true, List[Literal[...]]) instead of a dspy:pythonType primitive, per gepa_facilitysupportanalyzer's Literal/List[Literal] output fields. A field carries exactly one of dspy:pythonType, dspy:hasLiteralOption, or dspy:hasPydanticModelType." .

dspy:hasPydanticModelType a rdf:Property ; rdfs:range dspy:PydanticModel ;
    rdfs:comment "Renders the field's type as a generated pydantic.BaseModel class name instead of a dspy:pythonType primitive or dspy:hasLiteralOption Literal. Valid on both dspy:InputField and dspy:OutputField (no single rdfs:domain given, same pattern as dspy:pythonType/dspy:name -- actual validity is enforced by the admission gate). A field carries exactly one of dspy:pythonType, dspy:hasLiteralOption, or dspy:hasPydanticModelType." .

dspy:pydanticClassName a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:PydanticModel ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "Python class name for the generated pydantic.BaseModel subclass. Must be a valid Python identifier." .

dspy:hasModelField a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:PydanticModel ; rdfs:range dspy:PydanticModelField .

dspy:isListType a rdf:Property ; rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:comment "Only meaningful alongside dspy:hasLiteralOption: true renders List[Literal[...]], absent/false renders Literal[...]." .

dspy:optionIndex a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:LiteralOption ; rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    rdfs:comment "Zero-based, non-negative position of this option within its field's Literal[...]." .
dspy:optionValue a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:LiteralOption ; rdfs:range xsd:string .

dspy:geInt a rdf:Property ; rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    rdfs:comment "Only valid when dspy:pythonType is \"int\": lower bound passed as OutputField(ge=...), per gepa_trusted_monitor's suspicion_score field." .
dspy:leInt a rdf:Property ; rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    rdfs:comment "Only valid when dspy:pythonType is \"int\": upper bound passed as OutputField(le=...), per gepa_trusted_monitor's suspicion_score field." .

# ── Module properties ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

dspy:kind a rdf:Property ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "For a Module: one of Predict, ChainOfThought, ReAct, ProgramOfThought, MultiChainComparison, RLM, CodeAct, BestOfN, Refine, Pipeline, MultiHop, KNN, Parallel. For an Optimizer: one of GEPA, GRPO, BootstrapFewShot, BootstrapFewShotWithRandomSearch, BootstrapFewShotWithOptuna, BootstrapFinetune, COPRO, SignatureOptimizer, MIPROv2, AvatarOptimizer, BetterTogether, InferRules, SIMBA, LabeledFewShot, Ensemble, KNNFewShot." .

dspy:signature a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Module ; rdfs:range dspy:Signature ;
    rdfs:comment "Required for Predict/ChainOfThought/ReAct/ProgramOfThought/MultiChainComparison/RLM/CodeAct. Mutually exclusive with dspy:wrapsModule (BestOfN/Refine), dspy:hasStep (Pipeline), dspy:hopQuerySignature/dspy:hopAnswerSignature (MultiHop), dspy:trainsetName (KNN), and dspy:hasParallelStep (Parallel) -- each of those kinds uses its own composition/construction shape instead of a single bound Signature." .

dspy:usesMCPServer a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Module ; rdfs:range dspy:MCPServerConnection ;
    rdfs:comment "Admitted only when dspy:kind is ReAct. Wires the module to the MCP server whose tools dspy.Tool.from_mcp_tool() converts at call time." .

dspy:maxIters a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Module ; rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    rdfs:comment "ReAct/ProgramOfThought/CodeAct-only, positive integer. dspy.ReAct's real 'max_iters' (default 20), dspy.ProgramOfThought's real 'max_iters' (default 3), dspy.CodeAct's real 'max_iters' (default 5) -- confirmed by inspecting all three real constructors." .

dspy:comparisonM a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Module ; rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    rdfs:comment "MultiChainComparison-only, positive integer. dspy.MultiChainComparison's real 'M' parameter (default 3): number of reasoning attempts compared." .

dspy:comparisonTemperature a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Module ; rdfs:range xsd:double ;
    rdfs:comment "MultiChainComparison-only. dspy.MultiChainComparison's real 'temperature' parameter (default 0.7)." .

dspy:maxIterations a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Module ; rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    rdfs:comment "RLM-only, positive integer. dspy.RLM's real 'max_iterations' parameter (default 20) -- distinct from dspy:maxIters (ReAct/ProgramOfThought/CodeAct's 'max_iters'), because dspy.RLM's real constructor names it differently." .

dspy:maxLlmCalls a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Module ; rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    rdfs:comment "RLM-only, positive integer. dspy.RLM's real 'max_llm_calls' parameter (default 50)." .

dspy:maxOutputChars a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Module ; rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    rdfs:comment "RLM-only, positive integer. dspy.RLM's real 'max_output_chars' parameter (default 100000)." .

dspy:verboseFlag a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Module ; rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:comment "RLM-only. dspy.RLM's real 'verbose' parameter (default False)." .

dspy:hasLocalTool a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Module ; rdfs:range dspy:LocalTool ;
    rdfs:comment "CodeAct-only, required (dspy.CodeAct's real 'tools' parameter has no default -- at least one must be declared). Each renders as a scaffolded stub function passed in tools=[...]." .

dspy:wrapsModule a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Module ; rdfs:range dspy:Module ;
    rdfs:comment "BestOfN/Refine-only, required. dspy.BestOfN's and dspy.Refine's real 'module' parameter (both have no default) -- the Module instance being wrapped. Mutually exclusive with dspy:signature." .

dspy:rewardFunction a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Module ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "BestOfN/Refine-only, required Python identifier. dspy.BestOfN's and dspy.Refine's real 'reward_fn' parameter (both have no default) -- ggen scaffolds a NotImplementedError stub, the metric-function boundary." .

dspy:refineN a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Module ; rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    rdfs:comment "BestOfN/Refine-only, required positive integer. dspy.BestOfN's and dspy.Refine's real 'N' parameter (both have no default)." .

dspy:refineThreshold a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Module ; rdfs:range xsd:double ;
    rdfs:comment "BestOfN/Refine-only, required. dspy.BestOfN's and dspy.Refine's real 'threshold' parameter (both have no default)." .

dspy:refineFailCount a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Module ; rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    rdfs:comment "BestOfN/Refine-only, optional non-negative integer. dspy.BestOfN's and dspy.Refine's real 'fail_count' parameter (default None)." .

# ── Pipeline / MultiHop / KNN / Parallel Module properties ────────────────────
# Added 2026-08-10: composition and retrieval support. Every pattern below was actually
# constructed and executed against the real installed dspy 3.1.3 this session (RAG module via
# self.retrieve -> self.generate_answer; a 2-hop query-gen/retrieve/accumulate/answer-gen loop;
# real dspy.KNN/dspy.Parallel construction+execution), not assumed to work from docs.

dspy:hasStep a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Module ; rdfs:range dspy:PipelineStep ;
    rdfs:comment "Pipeline-only, required (at least 2 steps -- a single-step Pipeline is just that step's own kind). Ordered by dspy:stepIndex." .

dspy:pipelineSignature a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Module ; rdfs:range dspy:Signature ;
    rdfs:comment "Pipeline-only, required. Types the composed Module's own external forward() -- its input fields become forward()'s parameters (bindable via dspy:argSourceKind \"PipelineInput\"), its output fields become the returned dspy.Prediction's fields." .

dspy:stepIndex a rdf:Property ; rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    rdfs:comment "Zero-based, non-negative ordering position. Domain varies: dspy:PipelineStep (order within a Pipeline's dspy:hasStep), dspy:ParallelStep (order within a Parallel's dspy:hasParallelStep), or dspy:EnsembleMember (order within an Ensemble's dspy:hasEnsembleMember)." .

dspy:stepVarName a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:PipelineStep ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "Required. Python identifier -- becomes self.<stepVarName> in __init__ and the local variable capturing this step's call result in forward()." .

dspy:stepKind a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:PipelineStep ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "Required. Either \"Retrieve\" (dspy.Retrieve, requires dspy:retrieveK, no dspy:stepSignature) or any admitted Signature-bound leaf Module kind (Predict, ChainOfThought, ReAct, ProgramOfThought, MultiChainComparison, RLM, CodeAct -- requires dspy:stepSignature)." .

dspy:stepSignature a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:PipelineStep ; rdfs:range dspy:Signature ;
    rdfs:comment "Required unless dspy:stepKind is \"Retrieve\". Mutually exclusive with dspy:retrieveK on the same step." .

dspy:retrieveK a rdf:Property ; rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    rdfs:comment "Positive integer. dspy.Retrieve's real 'k' parameter (default 3, verified via inspect.signature(dspy.Retrieve.__init__), dspy 3.1.3). Domain varies: dspy:PipelineStep (only when dspy:stepKind is \"Retrieve\") or a Module of dspy:kind \"MultiHop\" (the shared retrieval k across all hops)." .

dspy:hasArgBinding a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:PipelineStep ; rdfs:range dspy:ArgBinding ;
    rdfs:comment "Optional (0+). The kwargs passed to this step's call in forward(). A Retrieve step never needs one (its call is always self.<stepVarName>(<the field bound as its query>).passages, resolved the same way); Signature-bound steps use these to wire each Signature input field to its real source." .

dspy:argName a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:ArgBinding ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "Required. The kwarg name -- must match one of the target step's dspy:stepSignature input field names (Retrieve steps bind their one positional query arg the same way, keyed by the field name)." .

dspy:argSourceKind a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:ArgBinding ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "Required. One of \"PipelineInput\" (the value comes from the Pipeline Module's own dspy:pipelineSignature input field named by dspy:argSourceField) or \"StepOutput\" (the value comes from dspy:argSourceStep's result, field named by dspy:argSourceField -- e.g. a Retrieve step's \"passages\")." .

dspy:argSourceField a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:ArgBinding ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "Required. The source field name -- a dspy:pipelineSignature input field name (PipelineInput) or the producing step's output field name / \"passages\" for a Retrieve step (StepOutput)." .

dspy:argSourceStep a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:ArgBinding ; rdfs:range dspy:PipelineStep ;
    rdfs:comment "Required only when dspy:argSourceKind is \"StepOutput\" -- the producing dspy:PipelineStep. Must have a lower dspy:stepIndex than the binding's own step (a step can only consume an earlier step's output, matching how the verified RAG/multi-hop forward() bodies are ordered)." .

dspy:hopQuerySignature a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Module ; rdfs:range dspy:Signature ;
    rdfs:comment "MultiHop-only, required. Types the per-hop query-generation ChainOfThought (the verified recipe's self.generate_query, real signature shape 'context, question -> query')." .

dspy:hopAnswerSignature a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Module ; rdfs:range dspy:Signature ;
    rdfs:comment "MultiHop-only, required. Types the final answer-generation ChainOfThought (the verified recipe's self.generate_answer, real signature shape 'context, question -> answer')." .

dspy:maxHops a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Module ; rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    rdfs:comment "MultiHop-only, required positive integer. The verified recipe's max_hops -- how many times the query-gen/retrieve/accumulate loop runs before the final answer-generation call." .

dspy:trainsetName a rdf:Property ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "Required Python identifier naming a consumer-defined list[dspy.Example] variable. dspy.KNN's and dspy.KNNFewShot's real 'trainset' parameter (both have no default) -- real Example data is arbitrary, consumer-owned, out of ontology scope, the same boundary as dspy:metricFunction. Domain varies: a Module of dspy:kind \"KNN\" or an Optimizer of dspy:kind \"KNNFewShot\"." .

dspy:usesEmbedder a rdf:Property ; rdfs:range dspy:EmbedderConfig ;
    rdfs:comment "Required. dspy.KNN's and dspy.KNNFewShot's real 'vectorizer' parameter (both have no default), rendered as a real dspy.Embedder(...) construction via dspy:EmbedderConfig. Domain varies: a Module of dspy:kind \"KNN\" or an Optimizer of dspy:kind \"KNNFewShot\"." .

dspy:hasParallelStep a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Module ; rdfs:range dspy:ParallelStep ;
    rdfs:comment "Parallel-only, required (at least 1). Ordered by dspy:stepIndex -- the modules ggen scaffolds into the exec_pairs list dspy.Parallel's real forward() consumes." .

dspy:parallelNumThreads a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Module ; rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    rdfs:comment "Parallel-only, optional positive integer. dspy.Parallel's real 'num_threads' parameter (default None) -- a distinct property from dspy:numThreads (Optimizer-only: GEPA/GRPO) because dspy.Parallel is a dspy:Module, not a dspy:Optimizer." .

dspy:parallelMaxErrors a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Module ; rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    rdfs:comment "Parallel-only, optional non-negative integer. dspy.Parallel's real 'max_errors' parameter (default None)." .

dspy:accessExamples a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Module ; rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:comment "Parallel-only, optional. dspy.Parallel's real 'access_examples' parameter (default True)." .

dspy:returnFailedExamples a rdf:Property ; rdfs:domain dspy:Module ; rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:comment "Parallel-only, optional. dspy.Parallel's real 'return_failed_examples' parameter (default False)." .

